Package: harmony-server
Version: 0.0.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: marthofdoom <marthofdoom@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-venv, ffmpeg, roc-toolkit-tools
Recommends: pipewire | pulseaudio
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/marthofdoom/harmony
Description: Harmony music hub — headless server
 A federated, self-hosted music hub: an always-on HTTP API and mDNS mesh node
 that the desktop, web, and mobile clients talk to. This package runs Harmony
 headless as a systemd service (no GTK), installing the app into a private
 virtualenv under /opt/harmony.
 .
 The Python dependencies are vendored as wheels inside the package, so the
 install is self-contained (offline) on CPython 3.11-3.13 / x86_64; other
 targets fall back to fetching them from PyPI.
 .
 Inter-instance audio routing uses roc-toolkit (pulled in via
 roc-toolkit-tools) and needs a running PipeWire or PulseAudio server on this
 host to reach an output sink; the mesh, HTTP API, accounts, search, and
 streaming work without an audio stack.
